Enginehost: a Live2D Cubism Core that failed to load stays an error.

live2dmodel.load() set did_load before it had loaded anything. The first call
that failed (libLive2DCubismCore.so is not on the handheld, so SDL_LoadObject
returns NULL) raised, and every later call answered True with every csm*
function pointer still NULL. Live2DModel.__init__ then called
csmReviveMocInPlace through a NULL pointer: SIGSEGV at pc 0 on SDLThread, the
caller in the live2dmodel module (Love & Sex: Second Base, Ren'Py 8.5.3, on
the console, 2026-10-16; the game ships .moc3 models in three DLCs). did_load
now becomes true only after every function resolved, so each attempt fails the
same way and the game gets a Python exception instead of a crash.
--- a/renpy/gl2/live2dcsm.pxi
+++ b/renpy/gl2/live2dcsm.pxi
@@ -87,8 +87,6 @@ def load(dll):
     if did_load:
         return True
 
-    did_load = True
-
     cdef void *object = NULL
 
     if dll:
@@ -252,4 +250,6 @@ def load(dll):
 
     post_init()
 
+    did_load = True
+
     return True
